// Poolit: how a change gets from code to the live system, and how to roll back
// Diagram type: Flow chart (Eraser diagram-as-code)
//
// LEGEND  green = in place and used  |  blue = exists, run by hand  |  orange = planned

title Poolit delivery pipeline
direction down
colorMode bold
styleMode shadow
typeface clean

Developer [icon: code, color: green, label: "Developer or Claude session"]
Branch [icon: git-branch, color: green, label: "Feature branch on GitHub"]

// ---------------- Automatic checks (GitHub Actions on every pull request) ----------------

GitHub Actions [icon: github, color: green, label: "GitHub Actions CI (every pull request)"] {
  Backend job [icon: check-circle, color: green, label: "Express tests (18)"]
  Frontend job [icon: check-circle, color: green, label: "Frontend: typecheck, lint, 53 unit tests, both apps build"]
  Database job [icon: check-circle, color: green, label: "Database: apply all migrations on a fresh Postgres, run 7 test files (access control, pool rotation, photos, student view, retries, cash and fees, privacy)"]
}

// ---------------- Checks run by hand before risky switches ----------------

Manual checks [icon: clipboard, color: blue, label: "Checks run by hand (not in CI)"] {
  Student end to end [icon: play-circle, color: blue, label: "Student app on the new backend in Chromium, 13 checks"]
  Rollback check [icon: rotate-ccw, color: blue, label: "Student app on Express (rollback path), 5 checks"]
  Photo pipeline check [icon: image, color: blue, label: "Resize and upload in real Chromium, 28 checks including upload attacks"]
}

Review [icon: eye, color: green, label: "Pull request review and merge to main"]

// ---------------- Frontends and old API ----------------

Vercel [icon: vercel, color: green, label: "Vercel builds student, vendor and backend projects from GitHub"]
Switch [icon: toggle-right, color: green, label: "Student build setting VITE_BACKEND: express (default) or supabase"]
Live apps [icon: globe, color: green, label: "Live student app and vendor console"]

// ---------------- Database changes ----------------

Migration file [icon: file-text, color: green, label: "SQL migration in supabase/migrations"]
Apply migration [icon: database, color: blue, label: "Applied to the live project by hand, after approval, then verified"]
Live database [icon: supabase, color: green, label: "Live Supabase project"]
Fingerprint check [icon: search, color: blue, label: "Compare live against repo: columns, indexes, functions, permissions, storage rules"]

// ---------------- Planned ----------------

Staging project [icon: copy, color: orange, label: "Staging Supabase project: migrations applied by CI, tests run here first"]
Backup [icon: archive, color: orange, label: "Nightly encrypted backup to R2, restore drill"]
Keep alive [icon: heart, color: blue, label: "Keep alive ping every 3 days (needs 2 repo secrets)"]
Cloudflare Pages [icon: cloudflare, color: orange, label: "Move frontends to Cloudflare Pages (Vercel Hobby is non-commercial)"]

// ---------------- Flow ----------------

Developer > Branch: git push
Branch > GitHub Actions: starts on pull request
GitHub Actions > Review: all jobs green
Developer > Manual checks: before switching a backend or shipping photos
Manual checks > Review: results reported
Review > Vercel: merge to main triggers builds
Vercel > Live apps: deploy
Switch > Live apps: choose the backend per app, change the setting and redeploy to roll back

Developer > Migration file: write and test locally
Migration file > Database job: tested in CI
Migration file > Apply migration: after approval
Apply migration > Live database: apply_migration
Live database > Fingerprint check: verify
Fingerprint check > Developer: differences reported

Live database > Backup: planned
Migration file > Staging project: planned, before live
Keep alive > Live database: stops free plan pausing
Vercel > Cloudflare Pages: planned move
